Package: mac-phoenix
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: hfsutils
Description: Classic Macintosh emulator with web-based UI
 MacPhoenix boots Mac OS 7.x / 8.x / 9.x in a window or in your browser.
 .
 Includes a 68k UAE interpreter (default), a Unicorn-engine-based 68k/PPC
 backend for validation, and a KPX PowerPC translator. The browser UI
 streams the framebuffer over WebRTC (H.264 / VP9) or WebSocket
 (PNG / WebP) and routes mouse and keyboard input back to the guest.
 .
 An optional Rust net-bridge provides Unix-socket NAT networking via
 smoltcp; with --mitm-tls it can downgrade modern TLS so classic Mac
 browsers can reach today's HTTPS sites (requires a separately built
 legacy OpenSSL — see /usr/share/doc/mac-phoenix/).
 .
 ROMs and disk images are not distributed.
